Hamnix Micro feather-nrf52840 size patch to kernel/proc.ad.
Applied by scripts/mkroot.sh in build/feather-nrf52840/root only; the
committed file is unchanged.

Reason: the nRF52840 has 256 KiB of RAM for everything: kernel data, kernel
stacks and heap, the files in / and every running program's stack and data
(boards/feather_nrf52840/link.ld; programs' code stays in flash).

    argument buffer of spawn/exec (kernel heap, for the length of the
    call)                                    4 KiB -> 1 KiB
Every stage of a pipeline execs while the earlier stages run; a 4 KiB
block for each, on top of their kernel stacks and pipes, was what limited
a pipeline to four programs (tests/nrf52/, the probe in the report).
A command line's argv and environment strings must fit in 1 KiB here.

Only constants, array lengths, and messages that quote them change.
Generated by editing a copy and
    diff -u --label a/kernel/proc.ad --label b/kernel/proc.ad kernel/proc.ad <copy>

--- a/kernel/proc.ad
+++ b/kernel/proc.ad
@@ -69,7 +69,7 @@
 PROC_STACK_DEFAULT: uint32 = 8192
 PROC_STACK_MIN: uint32 = 1024
 PROC_STACK_MAX: uint32 = 0x100000
-PROC_ARG_MAX: uint32 = 4096         # argv and envp strings plus their pointer arrays
+PROC_ARG_MAX: uint32 = 1024         # argv and envp strings plus their pointer arrays (Hamnix Micro feather-nrf52840: was 4096)
 PROC_ARGC_MAX: uint32 = 64
 PROC_PRIO: uint32 = 4
 
